  "t": "Anyone who has published enough writing online can no longer assume that an unsigned text keeps them anonymous.",
  "src": "paper/sections/08_conclusion.tex"
 },
 "steps": [
  {
   "view": "known",
   "t": "Once a model is familiar with a writer, it is hard to stay anonymous.",
   "src": "paper/sections/06_discussion.tex",
   "more": {
    "t": "Even when a text is brand new, a model can identify its writer from what it learned about them elsewhere.",
    "src": "paper/sections/06_discussion.tex"
   }
  },
  {
   "view": "refusals",
   "fn": 1,
   "t": "Refusals are rare.",
   "src": "paper/sections/06_discussion.tex",
   "more": {
    "t": "Fable 5.2 and Opus 5.5 refuse most often, on under 2% of all documents (counting provider blocks and written refusals that decline to do the task at all) and mostly on public peer reviews.",
    "src": "paper/sections/06_discussion.tex"
   }
  },
  {
   "view": "rewrite",
   "fn": 2,
   "t": "We test paraphrasing as a defense against author identification, using Argon at medium effort to revise texts.",
   "src": "paper/sections/06_discussion.tex"
  },
  {
   "view": "para",
   "t": "Paraphrasing lowers accuracy, though more familiar authors remain easier to identify.",
   "src": "paper/sections/06_discussion.tex"
  },
  {
   "view": "defenses",
   "t": "Defenses are limited:",
   "src": "paper/sections/02_introduction.tex",
   "items": [
    {
     "icon": "chat-x",
     "t": "models rarely refuse these queries",
     "src": "paper/sections/02_introduction.tex"
    },
    {
     "icon": "eye-off",
     "t": "deleting one's online writing does not remove it from the weights of existing models",
     "src": "paper/sections/02_introduction.tex"
    },
    {
     "icon": "rewrite",
     "t": "rewriting human-authored text with AI only helps partially",
     "src": "paper/sections/02_introduction.tex"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "n": 1,
   "t": "Refusals are far rarer through the API than through Claude Code. Claude Fable 5.2 gives no answer on 323 of 1,258 Reddit comments through Claude Code but on only 14 (1.1%, 3 blocked by the provider, 11 written refusals) through OpenRouter batches pinned to Anthropic, which our results use.",
   "src": "paper/sections/06_discussion.tex"
